Package: rae3
Title: RAE Reimplemented: Recurrent Copy-Number Alterations in Tumour Cohorts
Version: 3.0.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Rodrigo", "Gularte Merida", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "gularter@mskcc.org",
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4383-2523"))
Description: A reimplementation, from the publication, of the RAE method of
    Taylor et al. (2008) <doi:10.1371/journal.pone.0003179> for mapping
    recurrent DNA copy-number alterations: per-tumour soft discriminators for
    gain, amplification, hemizygous loss and homozygous deletion, a unified
    breakpoint profile, a permutation background model with recombination-hotspot
    cleavage, and regions of interest. Works on 'QDNAseq' objects and on segment
    tables. Every choice the paper does not determine is a documented parameter.
License: BSD_3_clause + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.0)
Imports: Rcpp, utils, stats, graphics, grDevices, grid, tools
LinkingTo: Rcpp
Suggests: QDNAseq, Biobase, testthat (>= 3.0.0), ggplot2 (>= 3.5.0), ggrepel,
    ComplexHeatmap, circlize, vegan, png
